    "solution": "In rotational equilibrium the anticlockwise moment is equal to the clockwise moment:\n\n$$ \\overset{\\displaystyle\\curvearrowleft}{M} = \\overset{\\displaystyle\\curvearrowright}{M} $$\n\nThe child's weight $F_\\mathrm{B}$ turns the seesaw anticlockwise and the adult's weight $F_\\mathrm{V}$ turns it clockwise. Each moment is the force times the lever arm:\n\n$$ F_\\mathrm{B} \\cdot l_\\mathrm{B} = F_\\mathrm{V} \\cdot l_\\mathrm{V} $$\n\nThe gravitational force is $F = m \\cdot g$, and the gravitational field strength *g* appears on both sides and cancels:\n\n$$ m_\\mathrm{B} \\cdot g \\cdot l_\\mathrm{B} = m_\\mathrm{V} \\cdot g \\cdot l_\\mathrm{V} $$\n\n$$ m_\\mathrm{B} \\cdot l_\\mathrm{B} = m_\\mathrm{V} \\cdot l_\\mathrm{V} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad l_\\mathrm{V} = \\frac{m_\\mathrm{B} \\cdot l_\\mathrm{B}}{m_\\mathrm{V}} $$\n\nGiven values (B = the child, V = the adult):\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nm_\\mathrm{B} = 25\\ \\mathrm{kg} \\\\\nl_\\mathrm{B} = 2.4\\ \\mathrm{m} \\\\\nm_\\mathrm{V} = 75\\ \\mathrm{kg}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ l_\\mathrm{V} = \\frac{25 \\cdot 2.4}{75} = 0.80\\ \\mathrm{m} $$\n\n**Answer:** The adult should sit $0.80\\ \\mathrm{m}$ from the pivot.\n\n**General conclusion:** The heavier person must sit closer to the pivot. A shorter lever arm compensates for a larger weight so that the moments balance."
