    "solution": "The centripetal force is given by\n\n$$ F_C = \\frac{m \\cdot v^2}{r} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nm = 0.50\\ \\mathrm{kg} \\\\\nv = 6.0\\ \\mathrm{m/s} \\\\\nr = 1.2\\ \\mathrm{m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ F_C = \\frac{0.50 \\cdot 6.0^2}{1.2} = \\frac{18}{1.2} = 15\\ \\mathrm{N} $$\n\n**Answer:** The centripetal force is $15\\ \\mathrm{N}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** The centripetal force is not a separate force. It is the resultant of the real forces (here the tension in the string) and is always directed in towards the centre."
