    "solution": "In the limiting case the normal force (or the tension) is zero at the highest point, so the gravitational force alone makes up the centripetal force:\n\n$$ mg = \\frac{mv^2}{r} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad v = \\sqrt{gr} = \\sqrt{9.82 \\cdot 4.0} = 6.3\\ \\mathrm{m/s} $$\n\n**Answer:** The minimum speed at the highest point is about $6.3\\ \\mathrm{m/s}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** $v = \\sqrt{gr}$ is the classic critical speed at the top of a loop. If the car goes more slowly, it falls inwards and leaves the track."
