    "question": "In a lab, a toy cow is hung from a string and set in motion as a conical pendulum. The group measures the time for $10$ revolutions as $21\\ \\mathrm{s}$ and the height of the circular path below the ceiling attachment as $1.1\\ \\mathrm{m}$. What value of *g* does the measurement give?\n\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420.0 246.6\" style=\"max-width:420px;width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:16px auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(15,22,32,0.12);border-radius:6px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif\"><line x1=\"115\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"263\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"121\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"114\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"133\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"126\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"145\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"157\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"169\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"162\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"181\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"174\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"193\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"186\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"205\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"198\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"217\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"229\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"241\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"253\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"246\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"189\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"189\" y2=\"185.9\" stroke=\"#8a8579\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><path d=\"M 109.6 185.9 A 79.4 20.7 0 0 0 268.4 185.9\" stroke=\"#8a8579\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><path d=\"M 109.6 185.9 A 79.4 20.7 0 0 1 268.4 185.9\" stroke=\"#8a8579\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><line x1=\"189\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"268.4\" y2=\"185.9\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"189\" cy=\"30\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#0f1620\"/><text x=\"181.0\" y=\"95.5\" font-family=\"Poppins,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#8a8579\" text-anchor=\"end\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" paint-order=\"stroke\"><tspan font-style=\"italic\">h</tspan> = 1.1 m</text><circle cx=\"268.4\" cy=\"185.9\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#0f1620\"/></svg>",
    "answer": {
     "value": 9.8,
     "unit": "m/s²"
    },
    "solution": "The vertical part of the string $l\\cos\\alpha$ is the height *h* of the path below the attachment, so the period formula becomes $T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{h/g}$. Solving for *g* gives\n\n$$ g = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot h}{T^2} $$\n\nFirst the period (the time for one revolution):\n\n$$ T = \\frac{21}{10} = 2.1\\ \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nSubstitution:\n\n$$ g = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot 1.1}{2.1^2} = 9.8\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2} $$\n\n**Answer:** The measurement gives $g \\approx 9.8\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}$, very close to the table value $9.82\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** Only the height *h* and the period *T* are needed. The pendulum's mass and the radius of the path cancel. Timing ten revolutions and dividing by ten reduces the error in the timing."
