    "solution": "The frequency is the inverse of the period:\n\n$$ f = \\frac{1}{T} = \\frac{1}{2.0} = 0.50\\ \\mathrm{Hz} $$\n\n**Answer:** The frequency is $0.50\\ \\mathrm{Hz}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** The relationship $f = 1/T$ applies to all periodic motion: pendulums, rotation and waves."
